[{"id":"VRCE-2-11-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":1,"english":"Then as the mighty king was lying down in this unbeseeming and improper guise, like Yayāti dropped from the celestial, that lady, personating the ruin of the race, not fearing public odium, who had discerned danger from Rāma to Bharata, not having attained her wish, again addressed the monarch, concerning the boon he had promised to her.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"250c687f8daa025445ffdec264a7d47ade529aafe4ab8c7af1c5373ae53e0f5d","compact":"637d02a97729032d699967759d2aa713ea872f99579fa029290e92e02fe27285","nasal":"5b05b186fd6e011913b0f8934320f7242c3024a2f0299d1960d532379765e4fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":2,"english":"Then as the mighty king was lying down in this unbeseeming and improper guise, like Yayāti dropped from the celestial, that lady, personating the ruin of the race, not fearing public odium, who had discerned danger from Rāma to Bharata, not having attained her wish, again addressed the monarch, concerning the boon he had promised to her.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48387dec32f934ddcd13af3bb4400d1e3ab631ef78094705dbb858b3fbaa94e4","compact":"7cac7cacdd12c9098ee479fbc6b430dbf979357b8785ddf29c2f1ca2d33a8a96","nasal":"b8ebc3912152e33e29cb8849d65e2d2c88f2a58dd27ebe1b945707078d4d0217"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":3,"english":"You describe yourself, O mighty monarch, as speaking the truth and firm in vow. Why then do you hesitate to confer this boon on me?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63e1f5e7be1d35196dd585e98da6de20834ea8d7a98dcaac482d4d9d6d767774","compact":"661890596f34656b543969e225b48eeff230d1d5e7c6c79d1a8ee93cc866ac8b","nasal":"661890596f34656b543969e225b48eeff230d1d5e7c6c79d1a8ee93cc866ac8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":4,"english":"Thus addressed by Kaikeyi king Dasaratha, remaining stupefied for a while thus answered her in wrath.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.938,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b731cb7b14abd07ee7471f5dce7095fe87d5aa5935e9801066945376a94ed4f","compact":"17814a1b90ce19bb939d9379baa59d2fef713fd45779ecbca52069776854e748","nasal":"6e665608f0b12ac8ef48b8f147f6f7249d674992fdfcef09cae0d20987f6b5ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":5,"english":"O ignoble one! O enemy of mine! On my being dead and that chief of men, Rāma, repairing to the woods, do you, yours wish attained, become happy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.542,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1d0c14201f20e0a9b768f8d391b141fc25bb51c0a8550cc6ac8c9df909f56c84","compact":"ae8c949acb17718c03f6d3b607613e9ca8d0c06c62140ac0f957d2fd4878231c","nasal":"ce9fd7f9cfeb9a13f00743fa30ed96ae07503060061eafc7516c09015cab27d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":6,"english":"Even if I speak this truly, yet none will lend credence to it. And what will Kausalya say to me, when Rāma shall have gone to the forest? Having done her this mighty wrong, what shall I say to her?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.467,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-12-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"533387ce363918dbb30b2933b501928d047635523597474f902881b28e8ca149","compact":"0ca9425b1b9718aad1bc05ceb3aa3393d526eb863b4c91864129a3fc21eaeedb","nasal":"0ca9425b1b9718aad1bc05ceb3aa3393d526eb863b4c91864129a3fc21eaeedb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":7,"english":"As king Dasaratha was bewailing thus with a heart wrought up with grief, the sun set and night came on.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"249cc3871162b5b79621dc8d9ef9345eb42bbfc944e30235498ce9d4805e27a1","compact":"7bec754e7271fc988cd5720f661b683caeac21890aa756cdd6632eed4e96923c","nasal":"7bec754e7271fc988cd5720f661b683caeac21890aa756cdd6632eed4e96923c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":8,"english":"But although crested with the lunar disc, the night failed to bring comfort to the king, distressed, and indulging in grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a016ba4ef162ca56f07c1fa6cb3e18925898ddd49f2aef10bee80930bed9a70a","compact":"83db03104c75203210fa886d531fc2d84fded5c425ecf250204e0bc1a0297913","nasal":"a2afba2b57bd015ec8e777583cda2479a7728be2a5e350f8f83278f23907b191"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":9,"english":"Then the old king Dasaratha, with his eyes fixed at the sky, sighing hot, lamented in this strain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"562d5e056a029af5e36963fb8f6feff05cc55f42d0aadcdd904e97d3501d94ef","compact":"bb09693742f6f880c6b362a9f961131a482d4bf057722868bcfc4ed180ba7329","nasal":"bb09693742f6f880c6b362a9f961131a482d4bf057722868bcfc4ed180ba7329"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":10,"english":"Or do you speedily repair for I do not wish to see the hated and relentless Kaikeyi, who has brought this calamity upon me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.438,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1679c29f496be773d54604d85985c256873e98b0ee75d097ca5bb9963de970fe","compact":"fe5be8f13250255a2121caf756492e3e709f0f61884ab42626fced68e7e35697","nasal":"1856992c25361fea1957f4a3b57a2cd715a9e4956f37c00d70fb87be53901386"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-11-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":11,"verse":11,"english":"Having spoken thus, the kind conversant with the duties of Sovereigns again endeavoured to propitiate Kaikeyī, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.59,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-13-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2011011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7af35674d765b8daa145e25492549c566e0d3dbf3b050bb91445cd1d0114ded3","compact":"021b24a06af0489251098d61e465b68520786e4f